{"name":"Esper’s Fungus Green","hex":"#80f9ad","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"esper","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A person who practices the development of psychic ability.","A person who has extrasensory perception."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/esper"},{"term":"fungus","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A eukaryotic organism of the kingdom Fungi typically having chitin cell walls but no chlorophyll or plastids. Fungi may be unicellular or multicellular.","The flesh of such an organism."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fungus"},{"term":"green","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of grass and leaves; a primary additive color midway between yellow and blue which is evoked by light between roughly 495–570 nm.","A member of a green party; an environmentalist."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a green hue.","Sickly, unwell."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/green"}],"entries":[{"title":"Fungus","blocks":[{"text":"A fungus is any member of the group of eukaryotic organisms that includes yeasts, molds, and mushrooms. These organisms are classified in the biological kingdom Fungi."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fc/Fungi_collage.jpg/330px-Fungi_collage.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fungus"},{"title":"Green","blocks":[{"text":"Green is the color between cyan and yellow on the visible spectrum. It has 295–350 different shades. It is evoked by light which has a dominant wavelength of roughly 495–570 nm. In subtractive color systems, used in painting and color printing, it is created by a combination of yellow and cyan; in the RGB color model, used on television and computer screens, it is one of the additive primary colors, along with red and blue, which are mixed in different combinations to create all other colors. By far the 